# What must never reach the build context.
#
# `docker build` ships this directory to the daemon and every file in it can
# end up in a layer, so this is a confidentiality boundary as much as a
# performance one — a `.env` copied in and deleted in a later step is still
# readable in the image history.
#
# It matters more here than on the API. A Vite build **inlines** `VITE_*` values
# into the JavaScript every visitor downloads (see `env.ts`), so anything that
# reaches this build is public by construction.

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
dev-dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Credentials.
#
# The build gets its configuration from `--build-arg`, never from a file, so
# there is no reason for any of these to be in the context. See the Dockerfile.
.env
.env.*

# Generated by the PWA plugin at build time, and stale copies in the context
# would be served in preference to the fresh ones.
public/sw.js
public/workbox-*.js

# Version control and CI.
.git
.github
.gitignore

# Editor and tooling state.
.idea
.vscode
.claude
.impeccable
.eslintcache

# The knowledge-graph export. Large, generated, useless to a build.
graphify-out

# Documentation and deployment manifests.
*.md
vercel.json
docker-compose.yml
